  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Page Updates**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `VisitsPage.tsx` updates. Right now, I\'m working on the new state required for the calendar view sidebar. Specifically, I\'m defining a `selectedCalendarDate` state using `useState`, initially set to \"2026-08-11.\" I\'ve also identified the need for calendar-specific sidebar filters, which will also be managed with a state variable.\n\n\n**Defining Sidebar Filters**\n\nI\'ve established the state management for calendar sidebar filters.  There are now state variables for appointment status, with initial values, picture filters, and a team search query.  I\'m focusing on how these states will interact with the data and affect the calendar view.\n\n\n**Generating Calendar Dates**\n\nI\'ve been working on the date generation logic for the calendar view. I\'m focusing on creating an array of date objects that include the day number, date string, and a flag indicating if the day is in the current month.  I have also accounted for padding from the previous and next months to maintain the standard 7-day-week structure.\n\n\n**Calculating Calendar Board**\n\nI\'ve implemented a `useMemo` hook to filter and prepare the visits data for the calendar board. I\'m taking into consideration appointment statuses and picture filters to display only relevant visits. The filtering logic is now in place and working with the defined state variables.\n\nI\'m now focusing on calculating the calendar board week columns. The goal is to generate the weekday columns for the 5-day or 7-day view, and associate the correct dates to each column. The headers will be Monday-Friday, or Monday-Sunday. I\'m focusing on handling data for each date, and linking each visit to the appropriate weekday column.\n\n\n**Constructing Calendar Weeks**\n\nI\'m now creating the logic for the calendar board week rows. I\'m focusing on an array of dates from Monday to Friday. I\'m thinking about the helper function `calendarBoardWeeks` that will compute these weeks accurately. This logic considers the first Monday, by accounting for offsets. For example, the first Monday can be calculated by adjusting for Sunday and each other weekday. I\'m aiming to generate the array of dates for each week in the month.\n\n\n**Refining Calendar Week Generation**\n\nI\'ve refined the logic for `calendarBoardWeeks`. This function calculates 5 weeks, each containing Monday through Friday dates, generating an array of date objects. These objects include day numbers, formatted date strings, a flag for current month inclusion, and an associated visits array. The function adjusts to handle weeks that overlap the start/end of the month.\n\n\n**Validating Calendar Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the JSX for the Calendar View. I\'m taking a close look at the grid structure, specifically how the left sidebar and main calendar board are arranged, focusing on the column spans and responsiveness. I\'m reviewing how the mini calendar picker widget is incorporated into the sidebar.\n\n\n**Implementing Calendar Navigation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the calendar navigation controls. I\'ve integrated buttons for navigating to the previous and next months, updating `calendarCurrentDate` accordingly. I\'m also including a display of the current month and year in a readable format. The button elements include the proper logic, and relevant styles.\n\n\n**Constructing Mini Calendar**\n\nI\'m now building out the mini-calendar picker. I\'ve focused on generating the daily grid and using `miniCalendarDays.map` to create the structure for the month\'s days. I\'m dynamically updating the `isSelected` state, when specific dates are selected. I\'m focusing on the responsive design to ensure a good UI.\n\n\n\n**Refining Status Filters**\n\nI\'ve just added a \"Clear\" button to the filter section of the sidebar, resetting all status filters, picture filters, and the team search query.  This clears the filters to their initial defaults and updates the UI for a clean slate. I\'m making sure it works properly.\n\n\n**Implementing Status Checkboxes**\n\nI\'m now building out the status filter checkboxes in the calendar sidebar. I\'m focusing on the \"Completed\" and \"Confirmed\" statuses, including the checkbox input elements, labels, and the associated visual cues (colored dots). I\'ve integrated their state with `calStatusFilter` using `useState`, for managing the checked state of the boxes. I\'m verifying the input events and making sure the checkboxes update the calendar view appropriately.\n\n\n\n**Adding Planned Status Filter**\n\nI\'m now integrating a \"Planned\" status filter. I\'ve built the checkbox input element, label, and visual cue, connecting them to the `calStatusFilter` state. I\'m verifying the input event handler ensures accurate calendar updates when the \"Planned\" status is toggled.\n\n\n**Integrating Team Search**\n\nI\'ve integrated a team search query input field into the sidebar. I\'m dynamically filtering a list of users based on the `teamSearchQuery` state, ensuring a responsive search experience. The input updates the calendar data, displaying only filtered team members. I\'ve also focused on the input field styles and placeholder text.\n\n\n**Developing Picture Filters**\n\nI\'m now implementing the picture filters in the sidebar. I\'m dynamically generating the picture filter checkboxes, mapping through a list of users. Each checkbox includes the user\'s avatar, name, and an associated state managed using `setCalPicFilter`, where I\'m tracking whether the picture is selected. The layout includes labels and input elements for each user.\n\n\n**Constructing Calendar Columns**\n\nI\'m now generating the calendar\'s weekday headers. I\'m focusing on the responsive design, ensuring proper column headers (e.g., \"Wednesday,\" \"Thursday,\" \"Friday\"). I\'m implementing the JSX to dynamically display the weekdays.\n\n\n**Refining Date Selection**\n\nI\'m now refining the date selection behavior within the mini-calendar. I\'m focusing on ensuring the `isSelected` state accurately reflects the user\'s selected date, which updates properly upon interactions. I\'m validating the visual feedback for selected dates and making it consistent.\n\n\n**Styling Visit Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on styling the individual visit elements within the calendar. I\'m aiming to enhance the visual presentation of each visit entry within the calendar cells. I\'m focusing on incorporating the status dot, time display, and customer name, using Tailwind classes for improved clarity and user experience.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
