    thinking: "**Investigating Navigation Routes**\n\nI\'m currently looking into how the navigation buttons and routes connect to the process of creating visits, particularly within `VisitsPage.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m examining how the \"+ Schedule Visit\" button, which either opens a modal or directs to a creation page, is triggered within the component. My focus is on tracing the flow to understand the mechanism.\n\n\n**Defining New Routes**\n\nI\'ve moved on to solidify the new routing structure. I am considering `/visits/schedule`, `/visits/create`, and `/visits/new`. I\'m going to look at adding these paths to `App.tsx` and potentially making dedicated page components, perhaps `CreateVisitPage.tsx` or `ScheduleVisitPage.tsx`, in the `/src/pages/visits/` directory. Within `VisitsPage.tsx`, I\'ll implement navigation to `/visits/schedule` using `useNavigate()` or a `<Link>`.\n\nNext, I will review user specifications, considering the page name and layout.\n\n\n"
