    thinking: "**Designing the Schedule**\n\nI\'ve made great strides! The navigation now smoothly directs users to `/visits/schedule` from both the \"+ Schedule Visit\" button within `VisitsPage.tsx` and the `<Link>` component. The next step is to design and implement the `ScheduleVisitPage.tsx` component, which will be the dedicated page for scheduling.\n\n\n**Verifying the Page Requirements**\n\nI\'ve meticulously outlined the requirements for the \"ScheduleVisitPage\". I\'ve finalized the header and navigation structure, including breadcrumbs and the page title. The form layout will be a two-column desktop grid. Next, I am organizing the left column will contain visit details. This section starts with a searchable customer field, populated by a dropdown from the `DataService`. This will populate the location field. The date and time fields will follow.\n\n\n**Defining the Inputs**\n\nI\'m now detailing the individual form fields for the ScheduleVisitPage, specifically focusing on the input types and data structures. For the left column, I\'ve specified:\n-   **Date**: Date picker.\n-   **Start Time** and **End Time**: Time inputs.\n-   **Location**: Text input for the meeting address.\n-   **Visit Purpose**: Determined a select/dropdown, with custom input option, and defined options.\nI\'m now diving into the requirements for the right column and user search.\n\n\n**Detailing the Participants**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the right column of the form. I\'m fleshing out the \'Personal In Charge\' (PIC) selection, including the display of workload badges directly within the input box/card. Next, I am implementing the \"Additional Participants\" section, opting for a searchable multi-select dropdown that displays avatars and pill tags for selected team members. I\'m then implementing a notes section, with a full-featured text area. Finally, I\'m designing a dedicated visit summary card.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Visit Summary**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the visit summary card, incorporating key details: the time (start and end), location, and PIC. I also plan to add purpose and additional participants as badges. The actions bar is now fully defined, with buttons for \"Cancel\", \"Save Draft\", and \"Schedule Visit\". I\'m also cross-referencing and enriching user details for the PIC list and user data to ensure the most accurate data for the form. I\'m taking a look at the users in the `DataService` and the `initialData.ts` file now.\n\n\n"
