    response: "I have successfully completed the design and implementation of the **SalesFlow Pro Visit Detail web page**. \n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Header & Action Bar**: Built a clean header displaying the visit subject, customer name (\"PT Maju Jaya\"), and a dynamic status badge (e.g., \"Confirmed\"). Included core actions to **Start Visit**, **Reschedule**, or **Cancel** the visit.\n- **Horizontal Progress Timeline**: Implemented an interactive chronological timeline showing the visit\'s lifecycle from *Planned* \342\206\222 *Confirmed* \342\206\222 *In Progress* \342\206\222 *Completed*. The active state correctly highlights the current progression.\n- **Key Information Grid**: Created a clean 7-column bento-grid layout for at-a-glance information blocks for the Customer, Date, Time, Location, Purpose, PIC (with avatar), and Additional Participants (with an avatar stack).\n- **Lower Workspace Area**: Added comprehensive sections below the main details for managing **Visit Notes**, **Related Tasks**, **Related Follow-ups**, and an **Activity History** audit trail.\n- **Completion Workflow**: Implemented dynamic state rendering so that when the visit transitions to \"Completed\", a prominent amber banner appears displaying **\"Visit Report Required\"** alongside a primary action button to **Complete Visit & Submit Report**, prompting the final debriefing step.\n\nAll routes are fully configured and the app is building successfully!"
