  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the initial scope. I\'ve successfully identified the user\'s primary goal: to design a \"SalesFlow Pro Visit Report\" web page. The first requirement I\'ve pinpointed is the header format, including \"Visit Report,\" customer details, PIC, and the visit date. I\'m moving toward the other requirements.\n\n\n**Outlining the Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'ve nailed down the two-column desktop layout. The main form\'s taking shape, detailing the visit result, discussion, needs, opportunities, next actions, and attachments on the left. The right panel will summarize crucial customer and visit data. Bottom actions will include draft saving, follow-up task creation, and visit completion. There will be a post-completion confirmation.\nI\'m also working on app structure and routing and will create a new page component and update the app structure accordingly.\n\n\n**Implementing the Route**\n\nI\'ve decided to implement the route `/visits/:id/report`. I will update `VisitDetailPage.tsx` to navigate there, replacing the modal. I am working on creating `VisitReportPage.tsx`, utilizing `useParams` for the ID and `DataService.getVisits` for data retrieval, defaulting to mock data if the visit isn\'t found. The page will utilize state for form fields like `visitResult`, `discussionSummary`, and `nextAction`, as well as a submission state. It will use standard styling.\n\n\n"
