  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the **SalesFlow Pro Visit Report web page** as requested.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Header Structure**: The page begins with a clean breadcrumb navigation back to the Visit details, followed by the main title \"Visit Report\", and a sub-header presenting the *Customer*, *PIC*, and *Visit Date*.\n- **Two-Column Desktop Layout**:\n  - **Left Form Section**: Contains intuitive data inputs for the visit report. Includes a highly visible **Visit Result** selector (Successful, Follow-up Required, etc.), text areas for **Discussion Summary** and **Customer Needs**, a toggle for **Opportunity Identified** (which expands to reveal details), followed by **Next Action**, **Next Follow-up Date**, and an **Attachments** dropzone.\n  - **Right Summary Panel**: A sticky sidebar presenting a clean summary of the selected visit, including *Customer*, *PIC*, *Visit Date*, *Duration*, and its current status label. \n- **Bottom Actions**: Clear call-to-action buttons are housed in the sidebar summary for quick access: **Save Draft**, **Create Follow-up Task**, and the primary **Complete Visit** action.\n- **Success State Workflow**: When you click \"Complete Visit\", the form beautifully transitions into a full-screen **Success Confirmation** view, confirming the visit has been logged and allowing you to quickly return to the detailed history.\n- **Integration**: I\'ve successfully connected this to your new Visit Detail page workflow. Clicking the amber \"Complete Visit & Submit Report\" button when a visit is in progress will now route you directly to this clean, dedicated report page."
    modified_response: "I have completed the **SalesFlow Pro Visit Report web page** as requested.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Header Structure**: The page begins with a clean breadcrumb navigation back to the Visit details, followed by the main title \"Visit Report\", and a sub-header presenting the *Customer*, *PIC*, and *Visit Date*.\n- **Two-Column Desktop Layout**:\n  - **Left Form Section**: Contains intuitive data inputs for the visit report. Includes a highly visible **Visit Result** selector (Successful, Follow-up Required, etc.), text areas for **Discussion Summary** and **Customer Needs**, a toggle for **Opportunity Identified** (which expands to reveal details), followed by **Next Action**, **Next Follow-up Date**, and an **Attachments** dropzone.\n  - **Right Summary Panel**: A sticky sidebar presenting a clean summary of the selected visit, including *Customer*, *PIC*, *Visit Date*, *Duration*, and its current status label. \n- **Bottom Actions**: Clear call-to-action buttons are housed in the sidebar summary for quick access: **Save Draft**, **Create Follow-up Task**, and the primary **Complete Visit** action.\n- **Success State Workflow**: When you click \"Complete Visit\", the form beautifully transitions into a full-screen **Success Confirmation** view, confirming the visit has been logged and allowing you to quickly return to the detailed history.\n- **Integration**: I\'ve successfully connected this to your new Visit Detail page workflow. Clicking the amber \"Complete Visit & Submit Report\" button when a visit is in progress will now route you directly to this clean, dedicated report page."
