  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Team Tasks Page**\n\nI\'m now focused on the \"SalesFlow Pro Team Tasks\" page, a team supervision portal. I\'m modelling it after \"My Tasks\". I\'m creating `/src/pages/tasks/TeamTasksPage.tsx` and will add it to `App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Defining Team Tasks Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the \"SalesFlow Pro Team Tasks\" page\'s structure. Summary cards for total, overdue, due today, and completed tasks are on my list. The filter toolbar will provide search, PIC, status, priority, customer, and due date options. The main table will include checkboxes, task details, PIC, priority, status, due date, creator, and actions. Bulk actions are: assigning PICs, changing priority, and changing status. I will add a \"View Team Workload\" quick action button in the header. To populate the page, I will need some more mock tasks with different PICs. The existing `DataService.getTasks` might need to be tweaked or extended to handle this. I am now creating a `/src/pages/tasks` directory to house everything.\n\n\n"
