  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refactoring Tasks Section**\n\nI\'m currently reworking the Tasks section, since there\'s no stateful toggling of the menus. The existing implementation just unconditionally renders them. I\'m focusing on rewriting the code block, starting with the Task component to optimize the NavLink rendering. I am planning to remove the Navlink components as a first step.\n\n\n**Consolidating Task Sections**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"My Tasks\" and \"Team Tasks\" NavLinks into a unified section. I\'ve examined their different states and conditional rendering to identify opportunities for reducing code duplication. I\'m focusing on creating a cleaner, more generalized component.\n\n\n**Reorganizing Task Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now restructuring the task navigation. I\'ve placed a \"Tasks\" parent section under \"SALES,\" including \"My Tasks,\" \"Team Tasks,\" and \"Task Board.\" \"Team Tasks\" has been removed from the \"TEAM\" section. I\'ve decided on the \"assignment\" icon and am updating the routes accordingly. My approach simplifies the structure and improves clarity.\n\n\n**Refining Task Styles**\n\nI\'m now honing the styling of the \"Tasks\" parent section and its children. I\'m focusing on making the active state clearer, especially the background, text, and border for visual cues. I\'m integrating the conditional class assignments more smoothly. I am simplifying the logic for determining when the \"Tasks\" section is active, ensuring proper display for `/tasks`, `/task-board`, and `/team-tasks`.\n\n\n**Optimizing Link Rendering**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the NavLink rendering. I\'m taking another look at the conditional class assignments and have the goal of making them more efficient. I\'m also looking for ways to streamline the logic within the `className` attribute to ensure that the active state styles are applied correctly.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 165932760
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
