  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully designed and built the **Task Board** for a seamless Kanban experience.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Kanban Architecture**: Created a wide, horizontally scrollable layout perfectly tailored for desktop. I introduced the new **\"REVIEW\"** status directly into the system\'s core types to support the standard `TODO`, `IN PROGRESS`, `REVIEW`, and `COMPLETED` pipeline workflow.\n- **Interactive Drag and Drop**: Implemented native HTML5 drag-and-drop mechanics. You can intuitively drag task cards across columns. When a card is dropped into a new status column, the change is automatically applied.\n- **Activity History Tracking**: Whenever you move a task between columns, the system automatically logs this event (e.g., *Moved task from \"In Progress\" to \"Review\"*) into the global Activity History stream under your name.\n- **Comprehensive Task Cards**: Designed rich task cards that display the Task Title, Customer name, Priority (color-coded), Due Date (highlighting overdue items), Related Visit references (if any), and a prominent avatar of the Person In Charge (PIC). \n- **Filter Toolbar**: Included a clean, multi-criteria filter row above the board to easily slice the view by Customer, PIC, Priority, Due Date, and Keyword Search.\n- **Column Controls**: Each column features a dynamic task counter in the header and a dedicated \"+ Add Task\" button docked at the footer for quick additions."
    modified_response: "I have successfully designed and built the **Task Board** for a seamless Kanban experience.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Kanban Architecture**: Created a wide, horizontally scrollable layout perfectly tailored for desktop. I introduced the new **\"REVIEW\"** status directly into the system\'s core types to support the standard `TODO`, `IN PROGRESS`, `REVIEW`, and `COMPLETED` pipeline workflow.\n- **Interactive Drag and Drop**: Implemented native HTML5 drag-and-drop mechanics. You can intuitively drag task cards across columns. When a card is dropped into a new status column, the change is automatically applied.\n- **Activity History Tracking**: Whenever you move a task between columns, the system automatically logs this event (e.g., *Moved task from \"In Progress\" to \"Review\"*) into the global Activity History stream under your name.\n- **Comprehensive Task Cards**: Designed rich task cards that display the Task Title, Customer name, Priority (color-coded), Due Date (highlighting overdue items), Related Visit references (if any), and a prominent avatar of the Person In Charge (PIC). \n- **Filter Toolbar**: Included a clean, multi-criteria filter row above the board to easily slice the view by Customer, PIC, Priority, Due Date, and Keyword Search.\n- **Column Controls**: Each column features a dynamic task counter in the header and a dedicated \"+ Add Task\" button docked at the footer for quick additions."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
