    }
  }
  planner_response {
    response: "I have designed and implemented the **Create Task** page in SalesFlow Pro.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Two-Column Structural Layout**: Designed a clean, wide desktop form that naturally flows into two clear sections: \"Task Details\" on the left and \"Ownership & Timeline\" on the right.\n- **Searchable PIC Selector**: Built a fully custom, interactive dropdown for the Person In Charge. It dynamically retrieves all tenant users and allows seamless searching. It displays the avatar, name, and role for each user.\n- **Real-Time Workload Engine**: The PIC dropdown goes beyond a basic select by calculating intelligent workload metrics in real-time. For each user, it queries the backend task data and displays their active task count, overdue task count, and assigns a color-coded \'Workload\' badge (e.g., Low, Medium, Heavy) so you know exactly who has the capacity for new tasks.\n- **Strict Validation Rules**: Implemented error-state UI and form validation confirming that \"Every task must have a responsible PIC\" as well as requiring a valid task title. Attempting to submit without one throws a visible, inline error alert.\n- **Integrated Routing**: Connected the new route (`/tasks/new`). Re-wired the main \"Create Task\" button on your main Tasks page, as well as the \"+ Add Task\" button on the Task Board columns, to gracefully navigate to this new page instead of the old behavior. \n- **Action Footers**: Anchored a sticky action row at the bottom with options to \"Cancel\", \"Save Draft\", and \"Create Task\"."
    modified_response: "I have designed and implemented the **Create Task** page in SalesFlow Pro.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Two-Column Structural Layout**: Designed a clean, wide desktop form that naturally flows into two clear sections: \"Task Details\" on the left and \"Ownership & Timeline\" on the right.\n- **Searchable PIC Selector**: Built a fully custom, interactive dropdown for the Person In Charge. It dynamically retrieves all tenant users and allows seamless searching. It displays the avatar, name, and role for each user.\n- **Real-Time Workload Engine**: The PIC dropdown goes beyond a basic select by calculating intelligent workload metrics in real-time. For each user, it queries the backend task data and displays their active task count, overdue task count, and assigns a color-coded \'Workload\' badge (e.g., Low, Medium, Heavy) so you know exactly who has the capacity for new tasks.\n- **Strict Validation Rules**: Implemented error-state UI and form validation confirming that \"Every task must have a responsible PIC\" as well as requiring a valid task title. Attempting to submit without one throws a visible, inline error alert.\n- **Integrated Routing**: Connected the new route (`/tasks/new`). Re-wired the main \"Create Task\" button on your main Tasks page, as well as the \"+ Add Task\" button on the Task Board columns, to gracefully navigate to this new page instead of the old behavior. \n- **Action Footers**: Anchored a sticky action row at the bottom with options to \"Cancel\", \"Save Draft\", and \"Create Task\"."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
