  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully designed and built the **SalesFlow Pro Opportunity Detail** view as requested.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Comprehensive Header**: Created a rich, prominent header displaying the core opportunity details (Customer, Value, Stage, PIC, Expected Close), paired with high-priority contextual actions (Edit, Move Stage, Create Task, Create Follow-up) for quick operations.\n- **Visual Pipeline Progress**: Implemented an interactive, horizontal pipeline stepper that beautifully maps the current deal stage (Prospect \342\206\222 Qualification \342\206\222 Proposal \342\206\222 Negotiation \342\206\222 Won), complete with visual indicators for completed, active, and pending steps. I also added a distinct failure state for \"Lost\" opportunities.\n- **Two-Column Content Layout**: \n  - **Left Section**: Added structurally clear sections for Opportunity Information, Customer Information, Related Tasks, and Follow-ups.\n  - **Right Sidebar**: Designed an informative summary card that surfaces critical metrics (Value, Probability, Expected Close Date, Creator, and Update Timestamps), followed by a sleek chronological **Activity History** feed to track every touchpoint on the deal.\n- **Seamless Navigation**: Updated both the Kanban Pipeline cards and the List View rows in the main Opportunities page to route directly to this new detail view when clicked.\n\nYou can view the new design by clicking on any Opportunity name from the List or Pipeline views! Let me know what you would like to tackle next."
    modified_response: "I have successfully designed and built the **SalesFlow Pro Opportunity Detail** view as requested.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Comprehensive Header**: Created a rich, prominent header displaying the core opportunity details (Customer, Value, Stage, PIC, Expected Close), paired with high-priority contextual actions (Edit, Move Stage, Create Task, Create Follow-up) for quick operations.\n- **Visual Pipeline Progress**: Implemented an interactive, horizontal pipeline stepper that beautifully maps the current deal stage (Prospect \342\206\222 Qualification \342\206\222 Proposal \342\206\222 Negotiation \342\206\222 Won), complete with visual indicators for completed, active, and pending steps. I also added a distinct failure state for \"Lost\" opportunities.\n- **Two-Column Content Layout**: \n  - **Left Section**: Added structurally clear sections for Opportunity Information, Customer Information, Related Tasks, and Follow-ups.\n  - **Right Sidebar**: Designed an informative summary card that surfaces critical metrics (Value, Probability, Expected Close Date, Creator, and Update Timestamps), followed by a sleek chronological **Activity History** feed to track every touchpoint on the deal.\n- **Seamless Navigation**: Updated both the Kanban Pipeline cards and the List View rows in the main Opportunities page to route directly to this new detail view when clicked.\n\nYou can view the new design by clicking on any Opportunity name from the List or Pipeline views! Let me know what you would like to tackle next."
