  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Revising Activity Page**\n\nI\'m currently focused on rewriting `ActivitiesPage.tsx`. The goal is to perfectly align it with the user\'s need to track changes and activities across customers and sales operations. I\'m focusing on the \"Activity History\" header and filter bar, integrating them to offer a seamless tracking experience.\n\n\n**Defining Activity Data**\n\nNow, I\'m defining the necessary data structures and UI components for the activity timeline. Specifically, I\'m focusing on parsing the data returned by `DataService.getActivities`, ensuring proper display of each activity\'s details. I\'m prioritizing a desktop-optimized, vertical timeline view. I can parse \'type\' or \'subject\' to decide icons.\n\n\n**Designing Filter Controls**\n\nI\'m now designing the filter controls. I will implement a search input, an activity type dropdown, a customer dropdown, and a user dropdown, which can also be a \"PIC\" dropdown since userId is effectively the PIC. I\'ll also define activity types and color schemes, incorporating standard filters for ease of use. I\'m aiming for a clean and efficient layout for filtering and searching activities. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness.\n\n\n**Implementing Filter Logic**\n\nI\'ve just implemented the useState hooks for filter states: dateRange, activityType, selectedCustomer, and selectedUser, and initialized with \"ALL\".  I\'ve also defined activityTypesList as an array to make available to the user. Next, I\'m working on the `useMemo` hook to apply filters. I\'m focusing on efficiency and clarity in the filtering logic to make sure the app can scale as needed.\n\n\n**Refining Filter Logic**\n\nI\'ve refined the `useMemo` hook, focusing on the filtering logic. Now, I have a loose match for `activityType` to accommodate varied data. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness; the `activityType` filter loosely checks for inclusion in the subject or description. I also added a helper to determine the icon and color based on activity type or subject. This allows us to make it functional without perfect data.\n\n\n**Determining Icon Logic**\n\nI\'m now creating a function to determine icons and colors dynamically. It checks activity subjects and types to set the right visual cues. I\'ve covered \"visit\", \"task\", \"opportunity\", \"customer\", \"call\", \"meeting\", and \"note\". I\'m making sure it\'s adaptable for various data inputs. I\'m focusing on providing users with clear visual cues at a glance.\n\n\n**Designing Timeline Display**\n\nI\'m now creating a rich timeline component to display activity data effectively. I\'m focusing on extracting relevant information from the `Activity` data structure to match the prompt\'s structure. My goal is to create a clear, desktop-optimized layout with icons, activity subjects, entities, customers, details, and user information, alongside timestamps, providing a user-friendly and informative display. I will also incorporate visual cues for at-a-glance interpretation.\n\n\n**Implementing Timeline Display**\n\nI\'m now implementing the timeline display using a left-aligned, vertical layout for optimal business dashboard presentation. I\'m focusing on incorporating visual cues using an icon and color, and including entity, customer, details, and user info with timestamps for user-friendly display. I\'m leveraging Tailwind classes for responsive design.\n\n\n**Refining UI Components**\n\nI\'m now refining the UI components for the activity timeline. I\'ve focused on displaying the activity `type` and `subject`, and showing the `entity` and customer details using a grid layout, enhancing clarity. I\'ve used Tailwind classes for responsivity.\n\n\n**Refining Data Display**\n\nI\'m now refining the data display to add further meta-information. I\'m focusing on displaying entity type and description. I\'m leveraging Tailwind classes to ensure a clear and structured layout for the desktop UI. I\'m also adding date formatting, making sure that it renders well. I\'m focusing on providing users with context at a glance.\n\n\n**Finalizing Activity Display**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the activity timeline display. I\'ve integrated user avatars and names within the timeline entries for easy identification. I\'m focusing on the clarity and consistency of these details within the overall UI. I\'ve also incorporated the correct date formatting for improved readability. I\'m now making sure everything aligns for the user.\n\n\n**Updating Filter Functionality**\n\nI\'m now refining the filter bar to fully align with user requests, specifically incorporating a new \"PIC\" option for the user dropdown, which is now implemented using the existing `userId`. I\'m also implementing the date range and activity type filtering. The activity filter is now functional and user-friendly. I\'m focusing on ensuring intuitive selection and display.\n\n\n**Enhancing Filter Controls**\n\nI\'m now integrating new dropdowns into the filter bar for refined activity searches. These dropdowns are focusing on adding customer and user selections, enhancing the precision of filter queries. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness and intuitive filtering choices. I also implemented PIC user filter dropdown to replace the user dropdown, keeping the functionality, for clarity.\n\n\n"
