  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Webpage Scope**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the webpage\'s precise scope for \"Activity Detail\" in \"SalesFlow Pro.\" My current focus is ensuring it fully supports audit information, emphasizing accountability and traceability. I\'m aiming for a clean, intuitive layout that clearly presents all relevant data.\n\n\n**Refining the Activity Detail**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the required fields for the audit log design within the \"Activity Detail\" page. I\'ve confirmed we have the core `Activity` type, though I need to address the `previousValue`, `newValue`, and `metadata` fields. For the UI, I\'ll initially parse data from descriptions, or create mock/derived metadata, with a graceful fallback if data is missing. My next step will be working on the route setup.\n\n\n**Implementing the Route and Page**\n\nI\'ve just added the route to `src/App.tsx` and am now working on making the cards in `ActivitiesPage.tsx` clickable to route to the `/activities/:id` page. My focus now is on designing `ActivityDetailPage.tsx`. I\'m starting with a breadcrumb header and a title, then I\'ll move into the main content. I\'m planning a left-side layout for the core activity details and a change log, including plans for a visually appealing diff. I will initially use heuristics on the `description` field, but may use metadata for more accurate views.\n\n\n**Constructing the Page Content**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the content structure for the `ActivityDetailPage.tsx`. I\'ll organize key details into cards: the activity details, related context, and system metadata. The latter will be mocked if the data isn\'t directly available. For now, I\'ll leverage a basic description parser to simulate a diff view, with the flexibility to use a more sophisticated approach with metadata later.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Activity Type**\n\nI\'m now revising the `Activity` type in `src/types/index.ts`. I realized I need `changes` and `metadata` to be robust, and ensure proper rendering. I\'ll use `sed` to modify the file to accommodate these changes. I\'ll need to figure out the right format for the `changes` array for the UI.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 369689937
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
