  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully designed and implemented the **SalesFlow Pro Activity Detail** page to provide complete audit information and traceability!\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Clean Audit-Log Design**: Created a structured layout prioritizing accountability. The header clearly surfaces the core Activity Subject, Icon, Date, Time, and Description.\n- **Change Log Panel (Visual Diff)**: Built a dynamic difference visualizer. If an activity contains explicit field updates (like a PIC reassignment), it renders side-by-side cards highlighting the **Previous Value** in a red tone and the **New Value** in a green tone, clearly bridged by an arrow.\n- **Context Linkages**: Added a \"Related Context\" section that explicitly links out to the associated Customer (e.g., PT Maju Jaya) and the specific Entity (e.g., Task: Follow up quotation).\n- **Authorship & System Traceability**: \n  - Designed a prominent **Changed By** card on the right column displaying the user\'s avatar, name, ID, and a profile action button.\n  - Added a **System Metadata** panel to surface deep diagnostic data, including the precise Activity ID, IP Address, Device/Browser information, and Action Source (e.g., Web Dashboard).\n- **Mock Data Update**: I\'ve injected the exact \"PIC Reassigned\" mock activity into your timeline data, ensuring you can immediately test and visualize this new detail page exactly as requested.\n\nYou can view the new detail page by clicking on the **\"PIC Reassigned\"** (or any other) activity card in the Activity Timeline. Let me know what you would like to work on next!"
    modified_response: "I have successfully designed and implemented the **SalesFlow Pro Activity Detail** page to provide complete audit information and traceability!\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Clean Audit-Log Design**: Created a structured layout prioritizing accountability. The header clearly surfaces the core Activity Subject, Icon, Date, Time, and Description.\n- **Change Log Panel (Visual Diff)**: Built a dynamic difference visualizer. If an activity contains explicit field updates (like a PIC reassignment), it renders side-by-side cards highlighting the **Previous Value** in a red tone and the **New Value** in a green tone, clearly bridged by an arrow.\n- **Context Linkages**: Added a \"Related Context\" section that explicitly links out to the associated Customer (e.g., PT Maju Jaya) and the specific Entity (e.g., Task: Follow up quotation).\n- **Authorship & System Traceability**: \n  - Designed a prominent **Changed By** card on the right column displaying the user\'s avatar, name, ID, and a profile action button.\n  - Added a **System Metadata** panel to surface deep diagnostic data, including the precise Activity ID, IP Address, Device/Browser information, and Action Source (e.g., Web Dashboard).\n- **Mock Data Update**: I\'ve injected the exact \"PIC Reassigned\" mock activity into your timeline data, ensuring you can immediately test and visualize this new detail page exactly as requested.\n\nYou can view the new detail page by clicking on the **\"PIC Reassigned\"** (or any other) activity card in the Activity Timeline. Let me know what you would like to work on next!"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
