    response: "I have successfully designed and implemented the **Team Workload Dashboard** for SalesFlow Pro.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Comprehensive KPI Header**: Engineered a series of top-level KPI cards to provide an immediate snapshot of team performance, matching the exact figures you requested (12 Team Members, 48 Active Tasks, 7 Overdue Tasks, etc.). The *Overdue Tasks* card uses an attention-drawing rose-red accent to highlight urgency.\n- **Advanced Workload Table**: \n  - Designed an enterprise-grade data table mapping every metric requested: Active Tasks, Overdue (highlighted dynamically), Visits Today, Follow-ups, and Opportunities.\n  - Built interactive column sorting for **Workload, Active Tasks, Overdue Tasks, and Visits**, allowing managers to quickly reorder the team based on capacity or urgent backlogs.\n- **Visual Capacity Bars**: Inside the Workload column, I implemented intuitive, progressive visual bars mapping to each employee\'s workload percentage. They dynamically adopt semantic colors (e.g., Red/High for Citra & Ahmad, Green/Normal for Budi).\n- **Inline Action Controls**: Implemented the required management actions on the right side of the row (View Tasks, View Visits, Assign Task, and Reassign PIC) using clean, minimalist icon buttons. \n\nYou can view the new dashboard by navigating to the \"Workload\" section under the \"Team\" menu in the sidebar. Let me know what you would like to tackle next!"
    modified_response: "I have successfully designed and implemented the **Team Workload Dashboard** for SalesFlow Pro.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Comprehensive KPI Header**: Engineered a series of top-level KPI cards to provide an immediate snapshot of team performance, matching the exact figures you requested (12 Team Members, 48 Active Tasks, 7 Overdue Tasks, etc.). The *Overdue Tasks* card uses an attention-drawing rose-red accent to highlight urgency.\n- **Advanced Workload Table**: \n  - Designed an enterprise-grade data table mapping every metric requested: Active Tasks, Overdue (highlighted dynamically), Visits Today, Follow-ups, and Opportunities.\n  - Built interactive column sorting for **Workload, Active Tasks, Overdue Tasks, and Visits**, allowing managers to quickly reorder the team based on capacity or urgent backlogs.\n- **Visual Capacity Bars**: Inside the Workload column, I implemented intuitive, progressive visual bars mapping to each employee\'s workload percentage. They dynamically adopt semantic colors (e.g., Red/High for Citra & Ahmad, Green/Normal for Budi).\n- **Inline Action Controls**: Implemented the required management actions on the right side of the row (View Tasks, View Visits, Assign Task, and Reassign PIC) using clean, minimalist icon buttons. \n\nYou can view the new dashboard by navigating to the \"Workload\" section under the \"Team\" menu in the sidebar. Let me know what you would like to tackle next!"
