  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the design and implementation of the **Team Performance Dashboard**.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Comprehensive KPI Overview**: I structured a top-level summary displaying critical team metrics in seven concise KPI cards: Visits, Completed Visits, Tasks Completed, Overdue Tasks, Won Opportunities, Sales Value, and Conversion Rate. This gives managers immediate top-level awareness.\n- **Advanced Filtering Options**: Implemented standard management dropdowns directly below the header to allow dynamic filtering across Date Ranges (Today, This Week, This Month, Q3), specific Teams (Enterprise vs SMB), and individual Employees.\n- **Rich Analytics Canvas (2x2 Grid Layout)**: \n  - **Visit Completion (Bar Chart)**: Compares scheduled versus completed visits visually over time using Recharts.\n  - **Task Completion by Rep (Stacked Bar Chart)**: Analyzes on-time versus overdue tasks on a per-representative basis to quickly flag workload issues.\n  - **Opportunity Conversion (Donut Chart)**: A segmented donut graph categorizing opportunities as Won, Open, and Lost for an immediate read on pipeline health.\n  - **Sales Value Trend (Area Chart)**: Utilizes a smooth area gradient mapping the sales value trajectory throughout the month/quarter.\n- **Leaderboard Ranking Table**: Constructed a comprehensive employee leaderboard at the bottom, automatically surfacing team ranks alongside key metrics such as visits conducted, completed tasks, closed opportunities, and total sales value generated. \n\nYou can view the new dashboard by navigating to the **Performance** tab on your application! Let me know what you would like to work on next."
