    response: "I have designed and implemented the **Sales Report Dashboard** for SalesFlow Pro.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Comprehensive Filter Panel**: Developed an enterprise-grade filter panel allowing dynamic segmentation by Date Range, Team, PIC, Customer, and Opportunity Stage. Functional action buttons (Print, Export, Apply Filter) are strategically positioned in the top right.\n- **Executive KPI Row**: Structured a six-card KPI array surfacing critical revenue and pipeline metrics (Total/Won/Lost Opportunities, Pipeline Value, Won Value, and Conversion Rate), using semantic colors to immediately highlight positive vs negative momentum.\n- **Rich Analytics Layout**: \n  - **Sales Pipeline**: Utilized a horizontal bar chart to visualize the funnel progression from Prospecting to Closed Won.\n  - **Sales by Employee**: A clean bar chart comparing revenue generation across the team.\n  - **Sales Trend (YTD)**: A smooth area chart displaying revenue growth trajectories month-over-month.\n  - **Opportunity Status**: A donut chart illustrating the distribution of Won vs Lost vs Open opportunities.\n- **Detailed Data Table**: Implemented a comprehensive, dense reporting table below the charts to map granular opportunity details including the Customer, PIC, current Stage, monetary Value, Win Probability, and Expected Close date.\n\nThe new report is seamlessly integrated into the navigation hierarchy and can be accessed under the **\"Reports\"** section in the sidebar via the new **\"Sales Report\"** link. Let me know what you would like to focus on next!"
    modified_response: "I have designed and implemented the **Sales Report Dashboard** for SalesFlow Pro.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Comprehensive Filter Panel**: Developed an enterprise-grade filter panel allowing dynamic segmentation by Date Range, Team, PIC, Customer, and Opportunity Stage. Functional action buttons (Print, Export, Apply Filter) are strategically positioned in the top right.\n- **Executive KPI Row**: Structured a six-card KPI array surfacing critical revenue and pipeline metrics (Total/Won/Lost Opportunities, Pipeline Value, Won Value, and Conversion Rate), using semantic colors to immediately highlight positive vs negative momentum.\n- **Rich Analytics Layout**: \n  - **Sales Pipeline**: Utilized a horizontal bar chart to visualize the funnel progression from Prospecting to Closed Won.\n  - **Sales by Employee**: A clean bar chart comparing revenue generation across the team.\n  - **Sales Trend (YTD)**: A smooth area chart displaying revenue growth trajectories month-over-month.\n  - **Opportunity Status**: A donut chart illustrating the distribution of Won vs Lost vs Open opportunities.\n- **Detailed Data Table**: Implemented a comprehensive, dense reporting table below the charts to map granular opportunity details including the Customer, PIC, current Stage, monetary Value, Win Probability, and Expected Close date.\n\nThe new report is seamlessly integrated into the navigation hierarchy and can be accessed under the **\"Reports\"** section in the sidebar via the new **\"Sales Report\"** link. Let me know what you would like to focus on next!"
