  planner_response {
    response: "I have designed and implemented the **Visit Report Dashboard** for SalesFlow Pro.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Filter Navigation**: Built a comprehensive filter panel at the top, allowing managers to instantly slice visit data by Date Range, Customer, PIC, Status, and Visit Purpose.\n- **Top-Level KPI Overview**: Implemented five primary KPI metric cards for immediate context: Total Visits, Completed, Cancelled, Rescheduled, and the overall Completion Rate (using distinctive colors to signify outcomes).\n- **Rich Analytics Canvas**:\n  - **Visits by Date (Line Chart)**: Tracks the daily cadence comparing scheduled vs completed visits.\n  - **Visits by PIC (Bar Chart)**: Visualizes the activity output distribution across the sales team.\n  - **Visits by Status (Donut Chart)**: Segments outcomes into Completed, Cancelled, and Rescheduled.\n  - **Visits by Purpose (Donut Chart)**: Analyzes the strategic intent of field activities (Initial Presentation, Negotiation, Follow-up, Relationship Building).\n- **Detailed Log Table**: Beneath the charts, I constructed a comprehensive Visit Log table detailing the exact date, customer, assigned PIC, purpose, status, elapsed duration, and meeting result notes for granular reporting.\n- **Navigation Integration**: A new \"Visit Report\" link has been successfully mapped under the Reports section in the left sidebar, accompanying the Sales Report. \n\nYou can view the new analytics page immediately by navigating to the \"Visit Report\" link in the application! Let me know what you would like to work on next."
    modified_response: "I have designed and implemented the **Visit Report Dashboard** for SalesFlow Pro.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Filter Navigation**: Built a comprehensive filter panel at the top, allowing managers to instantly slice visit data by Date Range, Customer, PIC, Status, and Visit Purpose.\n- **Top-Level KPI Overview**: Implemented five primary KPI metric cards for immediate context: Total Visits, Completed, Cancelled, Rescheduled, and the overall Completion Rate (using distinctive colors to signify outcomes).\n- **Rich Analytics Canvas**:\n  - **Visits by Date (Line Chart)**: Tracks the daily cadence comparing scheduled vs completed visits.\n  - **Visits by PIC (Bar Chart)**: Visualizes the activity output distribution across the sales team.\n  - **Visits by Status (Donut Chart)**: Segments outcomes into Completed, Cancelled, and Rescheduled.\n  - **Visits by Purpose (Donut Chart)**: Analyzes the strategic intent of field activities (Initial Presentation, Negotiation, Follow-up, Relationship Building).\n- **Detailed Log Table**: Beneath the charts, I constructed a comprehensive Visit Log table detailing the exact date, customer, assigned PIC, purpose, status, elapsed duration, and meeting result notes for granular reporting.\n- **Navigation Integration**: A new \"Visit Report\" link has been successfully mapped under the Reports section in the left sidebar, accompanying the Sales Report. \n\nYou can view the new analytics page immediately by navigating to the \"Visit Report\" link in the application! Let me know what you would like to work on next."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
