  planner_response {
    response: "I have implemented the **System Settings** page for SalesFlow Pro.\n\nHere is a summary of the new page:\n- **Navigation & Layout**: Built a professional left-aligned navigation sidebar to organize system configurations into five distinct categories: General, Sales, Security, Audit, and Integrations.\n- **Form Controls**: Added clear input components with descriptive helper text beneath each setting to guide administrators on functionality (e.g., specifying that the session timeout logs users out after inactivity). \n- **Configuration Groups**: \n  - **General Settings**: Dropdowns and inputs for Application Name, Timezone, Date Format, and base Currency.\n  - **Sales Defaults**: Controls to standardize initial task priorities, expected visit durations, and a toggle for auto-closing dormant opportunities.\n  - **Security Policies**: Toggles enforcing strict password complexity rules (uppercase, numbers, special characters) and MFA requirements.\n  - **Audit Logging**: Data retention policies and granular event tracking toggles for visits, pipeline updates, and system access.\n  - **Integrations**: A clean connection hub to eventually wire up External SMTP, Calendar syncs (Google/Outlook), and messaging platforms (Slack/Teams).\n- **Save State UX**: Implemented a responsive \"Save Changes\" primary action button complete with an animated loading spinner that simulates configuration saving.\n- **Routing Integration**: Added a dedicated `System Settings` link nested beneath `Users` in the primary side navigation menu for quick administrative access.\n\nYou can access it by clicking on **System Settings** in the main left navigation under the **ADMINISTRATION** section! Let me know if there\'s anything else you\'d like to adjust."
    modified_response: "I have implemented the **System Settings** page for SalesFlow Pro.\n\nHere is a summary of the new page:\n- **Navigation & Layout**: Built a professional left-aligned navigation sidebar to organize system configurations into five distinct categories: General, Sales, Security, Audit, and Integrations.\n- **Form Controls**: Added clear input components with descriptive helper text beneath each setting to guide administrators on functionality (e.g., specifying that the session timeout logs users out after inactivity). \n- **Configuration Groups**: \n  - **General Settings**: Dropdowns and inputs for Application Name, Timezone, Date Format, and base Currency.\n  - **Sales Defaults**: Controls to standardize initial task priorities, expected visit durations, and a toggle for auto-closing dormant opportunities.\n  - **Security Policies**: Toggles enforcing strict password complexity rules (uppercase, numbers, special characters) and MFA requirements.\n  - **Audit Logging**: Data retention policies and granular event tracking toggles for visits, pipeline updates, and system access.\n  - **Integrations**: A clean connection hub to eventually wire up External SMTP, Calendar syncs (Google/Outlook), and messaging platforms (Slack/Teams).\n- **Save State UX**: Implemented a responsive \"Save Changes\" primary action button complete with an animated loading spinner that simulates configuration saving.\n- **Routing Integration**: Added a dedicated `System Settings` link nested beneath `Users` in the primary side navigation menu for quick administrative access.\n\nYou can access it by clicking on **System Settings** in the main left navigation under the **ADMINISTRATION** section! Let me know if there\'s anything else you\'d like to adjust."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
