  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Access Control**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `DashboardResolver` component. I\'m focusing on how access control is determined using `useAuth()` to check the user\'s role and tenant ID. Currently, the component checks if the user is a `SUPER_ADMIN` or part of the `SYSTEM` tenant to dictate UI render. I\'m considering potential improvements to this logic, such as a more generalized approach.\n\n\n**Refining Role-Based Logic**\n\nI\'ve clarified the rendering logic: `SuperAdminDashboard` is shown when the user is a super admin AND visits `/admin/dashboard`. For the tenant, `TeamDashboard` is shown via the route `/dashboard`. The current approach seems sound; the UI routing ensures the correct component is displayed based on role and path, reducing the need for extensive in-component role checks.\n\n\n**Adjusting Navigation Logic**\n\nI\'m now changing how the `DashboardResolver` component handles navigation to better manage the active state of sidebar links. Currently, super admins are redirected to `/dashboard` when logging in via `/`, but the sidebar link is `/admin/dashboard`, making it appear inactive. The updated resolver will now navigate to `/admin/dashboard` for super admins and `/dashboard` for tenant users. I also realize this will impact the tenant sidebar links, requiring them to point to `/dashboard`.\n\n\n**Revising Dashboard Component**\n\nI\'m now determining how `SalesDashboard` and `TeamDashboard` should be handled. Should a `TENANT_ADMIN` see `TeamDashboard`? The prompt suggests this. I see that the `DashboardResolver` should probably return `<TeamDashboard />` for `/dashboard`, but that might not be the correct setup if different user roles have their own dashboards. It\'s becoming clearer that `tenantId === \'SYSTEM\'` implies `isSuperAdmin`, and the component needs to reflect this connection.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 510224123
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
