  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Data Flow**\n\nOkay, so I\'m honing in on how data moves. Initially, it\'s just a `picId`. I\'ve clarified that `saveVisit` doesn\'t automatically trigger `addActivity`; the front end handles that. However, this is acceptable, since dynamically mapping via `getTasks` is entirely automated.\n\n\n**Synchronizing Visit Data**\n\nI\'ve got a breakthrough on syncing Visits and Tasks! By mapping Visits to Tasks in `getTasks` and Tasks to Visits in `getVisits`, any Visit created becomes a Task automatically, and vice-versa. This ensures perfect data synchronization! No infinite loop, because data is read directly from local storage. The `VS-TSK` ID won\'t cause problems, since any Visit edits are just saved back to `VISITS`, updating the generated Task seamlessly.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 348644148
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
