    thinking: "**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve made significant strides in optimizing data handling. The `getVisits` and `getTasks` functions now dynamically build cross-referenced data in memory, avoiding infinite recursion. These functions read directly from `getLocal` and, crucially, implement deduplication. As a result, when a user schedules a `Visit`, it\'s added to the `VIS` data structure.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Task Override**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the task merging strategy. The goal is clear: ensure user edits to dynamically generated tasks take precedence. Right now, `getTasks` prioritizes `visitTasks` and overwrites any existing tasks with the same ID, causing user edits to be lost. The approach involves swapping the order of array spreading in `combinedTasks` - placing the existing `tasks` array *after* the `visitTasks` array. This ensures user-edited tasks in the `tasks` array override the dynamically created ones from the `visitTasks` array. This will fix the override bug and allow manual edits to tasks.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 567488715
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
