    thinking: "**Considering Imports and States**\n\nI\'m in the process of considering the imports needed for `TaskBoardPage.tsx`, specifically including `Task`, `Customer`, `TaskStatus`, and `FollowUpType`. I\'m also adding states for the Follow Up Modal; placing this state below `draggedTaskId` seemed logical.\n\n\n**Defining Follow Up Modal State**\n\nI\'ve just finished implementing the state variables to manage the Follow Up Modal.  These states include `showFollowUpModal`,  `pendingFollowUpTask`,  `followUpTitle`,  `followUpType`, `followUpDate`, and `followUpNotes`, providing the necessary data for a functional modal. I\342\200\231ve also defined the columns structure, and begun the `tasksByStatus` implementation.\n\n\n**Implementing Task Grouping Logic**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the implementation of the `tasksByStatus` function, which now correctly groups tasks based on their status, excluding \"CANCELLED\" as per the specifications. I am also working on `handleDrop` to manage task status changes.\n\n\n**Handling Follow Up Interactions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the logic to manage follow-up interactions. I\'m updating the task status locally to \"FOLLOW_UP,\" and saving the changes to both the local state and the DataService. Subsequently, I\'m creating a FollowUp entity, detailing the follow-up information, including related task details and activity.\n\n\n**Finalizing Event Tracking**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the implementation of event tracking. The system now accurately creates an activity record whenever a task status is updated to \"FOLLOW_UP,\" detailing the updated task, the type of follow-up, and related user information. The code now handles the hiding of the follow-up modal, and clears its related state variables after an action.\n\n\n**Refining Modal Close**\n\nThe follow-up modal now closes correctly, and the state variables are cleared. The code now handles the hiding of the follow-up modal, and clears related state variables after an action.\n\n\n**Adding Follow Up Inputs**\n\nI\'m currently working on the input components for the follow-up modal. I\'ve just implemented the select input for follow-up types (Call, Email, Meeting, WhatsApp) using a controlled component with the `FollowUpType` enum. I\'ve also implemented the date input, to select a scheduled date, so the system is able to track a follow up date.\n\n\n**Implementing Follow Up Form**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `FollowUpModal` and have completed integrating the notes text area, and implemented the cancel and submit buttons. I am now working on connecting these inputs to the `handleCreateFollowUp` function.\n\n\n"
